summary:
  A dead import lands in shipped Python — the ruff half of the gate must say so.

history:
  The Python rules arrived 2026-08-09 (ruff.toml, ceiling zero) with the same
  worry every guard in this project has earned: a check can be wired, look
  green, and be dead. Two guards spent weeks that way. This mutant is the
  red-path proof for the ruff step in dev.sh lint — if that step is unplugged
  or its failure stops reaching the gate's exit code, this survives and the
  survivor report points here.

target:
  package/contents/ui/cast.py

find:
  import hashlib
  import http.client

replace:
  import hashlib
  import wave as _ruff_gate_probe
  import http.client

expect:
  The ruff step in scripts/dev.sh lint: F401 (unused import) fires on the
  probe, the step sets fail=1, lint exits red.
